# Copy to backend/.env, which is not committed.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
# The public name of the server. Leave unset on a laptop.
# DOMAIN=api.example.org
# Lets every account play the daily and see the boards. For trying things out only.
# EVERYONE_IS_SUBSCRIBED=true
# Client ids a sign-in token must be made out to, comma-separated. Google: the Android app asks
# Credential Manager for a token made out to the WEB client id (the one passed to the build as
# anatomypro.google.serverClientId), so that one must be listed. Apple: the native sheet's
# token is made out to the bundle id.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS=…apps.googleusercontent.com
# APPLE_CLIENT_IDS=com.ptk.anatomypro

# --- subscriptions (backend spec §8). All unset: nothing can be bought, nobody is a subscriber.
# What is on sale: product ids as created in BOTH stores, each with its period.
# PLANS=pro.monthly:monthly,pro.yearly:yearly
#
# Key files go in backend/secrets/, which is mounted at /secrets and is not committed.
#
# Google Play. All four, or none: the server does not start with some.
# GOOGLE_PLAY_PACKAGE=com.ptk.anatomypro
# The JSON key of a service account that the Play Console has given access to the app.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE=/secrets/play-service-account.json
# The Pub/Sub push subscription for real-time developer notifications must have
# authentication on. These are the audience it was given, and the service account it signs as.
# GOOGLE_PUSH_AUDIENCE=https://api.example.org/v1/webhooks/google
# GOOGLE_PUSH_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=play-push@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
#
# The App Store.
# APPLE_BUNDLE_ID=com.ptk.anatomypro
# Apple Root CA - G3, from https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/ (.cer or .pem). The
# server prints its SHA-256 fingerprint at start: compare it with the one Apple publishes.
# APPLE_ROOT_CA_FILE=/secrets/AppleRootCA-G3.cer
# Production only unless this says otherwise. A sandbox purchase costs nothing, so add
# Sandbox only where that is wanted — which includes the server App Review tests against.
# APPLE_ENVIRONMENTS=Production,Sandbox
# An in-app purchase key from App Store Connect, for asking Apple about a subscription near
# its expiry. Without it purchases and notifications still work; the re-check skips Apple.
# APPLE_API_KEY_FILE=/secrets/AuthKey_ABC123DEFG.p8
# APPLE_API_KEY_ID=ABC123DEFG
# APPLE_API_ISSUER_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#
# How often subscriptions near their expiry are asked about again. 0 turns it off.
# RECHECK_EVERY_HOURS=6
